            },
            "chunk_type": "segment",
            "content": "North America sales increased 10% in 2025, compared to the prior year. The sales growth primarily reflects increased unit sales, including sales by third-party sellers, advertising sales, and subscription services.",
            "entity_name": "AMZN North America Segment",
            "entity_type_entity": "RevenueSegment",
            "valid_from": "2026-02-05",
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_7_MDA"
            },
            "chunk_type": "segment",
            "content": "International sales increased 13% in 2025, compared to the prior year. The sales growth primarily reflects increased unit sales, including sales by third-party sellers, advertising sales, and subscription services.",
            "entity_name": "AMZN International Segment",
            "entity_type_entity": "RevenueSegment",
            "valid_from": "2026-02-05",
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_7_MDA"
            },
            "chunk_type": "segment",
            "content": "AWS sales increased 20% in 2025, compared to the prior year. The sales growth primarily reflects increased customer usage, partially offset by pricing changes primarily driven by long-term customer contracts.",
            "entity_name": "AMZN AWS Segment",
            "entity_type_entity": "RevenueSegment",
            "valid_from": "2026-02-05",
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_7_MDA",
              "update_type": "initiation"
            },
            "chunk_type": "guidance",
            "content": "Net sales are expected to be between $173.5 billion and $178.5 billion, or to grow between 11% and 15% compared with first quarter 2025. This guidance anticipates a favorable impact of approximately 180 basis points from foreign exchange rates.",
            "entity_name": "AMZN Q1 2026 Net Sales Guidance",
            "entity_type_entity": "GuidanceUpdate",
            "valid_from": "2026-02-05",
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_7_MDA",
              "update_type": "initiation"
            },
            "chunk_type": "guidance",
            "content": "Operating income is expected to be between $16.5 billion and $21.5 billion, compared with $18.4 billion in first quarter 2025. This guidance includes approximately $1 billion of higher year-over-year Amazon Leo costs as we scale in 2026, as well as investment in quick commerce and even sharper prices in our international stores business.",
            "entity_name": "AMZN Q1 2026 Operating Income Guidance",
            "entity_type_entity": "GuidanceUpdate",
            "valid_from": "2026-02-05",
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_7_MDA"
            },
            "chunk_type": "legal_proceeding",
            "content": "Operating income for 2025 includes charges of $2.5 billion we recorded in Q3 2025 related to the settlement of a lawsuit with the FTC and $2.7 billion, of which $1.8 billion was recorded in Q3 2025, of estimated severance costs primarily related to planned role eliminations.",
            "entity_name": "Amazon FTC Lawsuit Settlement",
            "entity_type_entity": "LegalProceeding",
            "valid_from": "2026-02-05",
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_7_MDA"
            },
            "chunk_type": "material_event",
            "content": "Operating income for 2025 includes charges of $2.5 billion we recorded in Q3 2025 related to the settlement of a lawsuit with the FTC and $2.7 billion, of which $1.8 billion was recorded in Q3 2025, of estimated severance costs primarily related to planned role eliminations.",
            "entity_name": "AMZN 2025 Workforce Restructuring",
            "entity_type_entity": "MaterialEvent",
            "valid_from": "2026-02-05",
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_7_MDA"
            },
            "chunk_type": "capital_structure_event",
            "content": "Cash inflows from financing activities resulted from proceeds from short-term debt, and other and long-term-debt of $5.1 billion and $25.0 billion in 2024 and 2025.",
